 Tetrahedralization Schemes decompose cubic voxel cells into tetrahedra to facilitate isosurface extraction, addressing topological ambiguities and artifacts inherent in standard cube-based methods like Marching Cubes [S2, unofficial]. This family focuses on the geometric partitioning strategy itself—determining vertex counts, tetrahedron shapes, and neighbor dependencies [S1, unofficial]. It sets itself apart by offering alternatives to the standard 5-tetrahedron or 6-tetrahedron decompositions, such as schemes using 12 or 24 tetrahedra, or those based on non-cubic lattices like BCC or Diamond, to improve surface smoothness or reduce lookup table memory [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
 ## Shared principles
-The core mechanism replaces the standard cubic voxel with a set of non-overlapping tetrahedra that fill the same volume [S1, unofficial]. For each tetrahedron, the scalar field values at its four vertices determine the intersection with an isosurface threshold $T$ [S2, unofficial]. The algorithm checks the sign of $(S_i - T)$ for each vertex $i$ [Parent]. If signs differ across an edge, linear interpolation finds the intersection point $P$:
+The core mechanism replaces the standard cubic voxel with a set of non-overlapping tetrahedra that fill the same volume [S1, unofficial]. For each tetrahedron, the scalar field values at its four vertices determine the intersection with an isosurface threshold $T$ [S2, unofficial]. The algorithm checks the sign of $(S_i - T)$ for each vertex $i$ [S1, unofficial]. If signs differ across an edge, linear interpolation finds the intersection point $P$:
 $$ P = V_1 + \frac{T - S_1}{S_2 - S_1} (V_2 - V_1) $$
-where $V_1, V_2$ are vertex positions and $S_1, S_2$ are scalar values [Parent]. The collection of these points forms the output triangle mesh vertices [S1, unofficial]. The specific scheme dictates tetrahedron connectivity, whether new "fabricated" points (like cell centers) are introduced, and how adjacent cells share boundaries to ensure a manifold mesh [S1, unofficial][S2, unofficial].
